{"id":"ALG-P09","workedExamples":[{"id":"ALG-P09-we-01","title":"Square a binomial sum: expand (x + 5)^2","steps":[{"prompt":"We want (x + 5)^2. A very common error is to square each piece and write x^2 + 25. Why is that wrong?","reveal":"(x + 5)^2 means (x + 5)(x + 5) — the whole sum multiplied by itself, NOT x^2 + 5^2. Squaring a sum is not the same as squaring each term. We must multiply it all out."},{"prompt":"Multiply (x + 5)(x + 5) term by term (think of the area of a square with side x + 5). What four products appear?","reveal":"x·x = x^2, x·5 = 5x, 5·x = 5x, and 5·5 = 25. The square's area splits into x^2, two equal 5x rectangles, and 25."},{"prompt":"Combine the two middle products 5x and 5x. What is the middle term?","reveal":"5x + 5x = 10x. There are TWO of them, so the middle term is 2·(x·5) = 10x. This is the term the wrong answer x^2 + 25 leaves out."},{"prompt":"Write the full expansion and name the pattern.","reveal":"(x + 5)^2 = x^2 + 10x + 25. Pattern: (a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2. The 2ab middle term is essential — a perfect square is never just a^2 + b^2."},{"prompt":"Quick check: is x^2 + 25 ever equal to (x + 5)^2?","reveal":"No. Try x = 1: (1 + 5)^2 = 36, but 1^2 + 25 = 26. They differ by the missing 10x = 10. The middle term is real and required."}]},{"id":"ALG-P09-we-02","title":"Multiply a conjugate pair: expand (x + 7)(x − 7)","steps":[{"prompt":"We want (x + 7)(x − 7). These factors are conjugates: same terms, opposite signs. What four products appear when we multiply them out?","reveal":"x·x = x^2, x·(−7) = −7x, 7·x = +7x, and 7·(−7) = −49."},{"prompt":"Look at the two middle products, −7x and +7x. What happens when we combine them?","reveal":"−7x + 7x = 0. They are equal in size but opposite in sign, so they cancel completely. There is NO middle term left."},{"prompt":"Write the full expansion and name the pattern.","reveal":"(x + 7)(x − 7) = x^2 − 49. Pattern: (a + b)(a − b) = a^2 − b^2, a difference of squares."},{"prompt":"A student writes x^2 + 14x − 49, keeping a middle term. Why is that wrong here?","reveal":"The middle terms only cancel because the signs are opposite (conjugates). There is no surviving 14x. Keeping a middle term confuses conjugates with a perfect square — they are different patterns."},{"prompt":"Warning: does the cancel trick work for (x + 7)^2?","reveal":"No. (x + 7)^2 = (x + 7)(x + 7) has +7x + 7x = +14x, which does NOT cancel. Only conjugates (opposite signs) lose the middle term; perfect squares keep 2ab."}]}],"problems":{"p1":[{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A square patch of infield dirt has a side of length (x + 4) feet. Expand (x + 4)^2 to get its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 8x + 16","x^2 + 16","x^2 + 4x + 16","x^2 + 8x + 8"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 8x + 16"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 16":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 4x + 16":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 8x + 8":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["(x + 4)^2 = (x + 4)(x + 4); it is not x^2 + 16.","Middle term is 2·x·4 = 8x. Answer: x^2 + 8x + 16."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"Two outfield distances form a conjugate pair: (x + 6) and (x − 6). Expand (x + 6)(x − 6).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 36","x^2 + 12x − 36","x^2 − 12x − 36","x^2 + 36"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 36"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 12x − 36":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 12x − 36":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["The +6x and −6x are opposite, so they cancel.","Conjugates give a^2 − b^2: x^2 − 36."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-baseball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A square section of the bullpen has side (x + 3) yards. Expand (x + 3)^2 for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 6x + 9","x^2 + 9","x^2 + 3x + 9","x^2 + 6x + 6"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 6x + 9"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 9":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 3x + 9":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 6x + 6":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Square the whole sum, not each piece; it is not x^2 + 9.","Middle term 2·x·3 = 6x. Answer: x^2 + 6x + 9."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-baseball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A coach compares (x + 8)(x − 8), a conjugate pair of base-path lengths. Expand it.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 64","x^2 − 16x − 64","x^2 + 16x − 64","x^2 + 64"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 64"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 16x − 64":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 + 16x − 64":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+8x and −8x cancel, so no middle term.","Difference of squares: x^2 − 64."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-softball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A square warm-up zone has a side of (x + 5) feet. Expand (x + 5)^2 to get its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 10x + 25","x^2 + 25","x^2 + 5x + 25","x^2 + 10x + 10"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 10x + 25"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 25":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 5x + 25":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 10x + 10":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["(x + 5)^2 = (x + 5)(x + 5); it is not x^2 + 25.","Middle term 2·x·5 = 10x. Answer: x^2 + 10x + 25."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-softball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"Two throw distances are conjugates: (x + 9) and (x − 9). Expand (x + 9)(x − 9).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 81","x^2 + 18x − 81","x^2 − 18x − 81","x^2 + 81"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 81"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 18x − 81":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 18x − 81":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+9x and −9x cancel out.","Conjugates give a^2 − b^2: x^2 − 81."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-softball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A square pitching grid has side (x + 2) feet. Expand (x + 2)^2 for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 4x + 4","x^2 + 4","x^2 + 2x + 4","x^2 + 4x + 2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 4x + 4"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 4":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 2x + 4":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 4x + 2":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Square the whole sum, not each piece; not x^2 + 4.","Middle term 2·x·2 = 4x. Answer: x^2 + 4x + 4."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-softball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"Compare the conjugate pair (x + 7)(x − 7) of outfield gaps. Expand it.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 49","x^2 + 14x − 49","x^2 − 14x − 49","x^2 + 49"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 49"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 14x − 49":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 14x − 49":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+7x and −7x cancel; no middle term.","Difference of squares: x^2 − 49."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-basketball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A square area of the court has a side of (x + 6) feet. Expand (x + 6)^2 to get its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 12x + 36","x^2 + 36","x^2 + 6x + 36","x^2 + 12x + 12"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 12x + 36"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 36":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 6x + 36":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 12x + 12":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["(x + 6)^2 = (x + 6)(x + 6); not x^2 + 36.","Middle term 2·x·6 = 12x. Answer: x^2 + 12x + 36."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-basketball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"Two shooting ranges are conjugates: (x + 5) and (x − 5). Expand (x + 5)(x − 5).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 25","x^2 + 10x − 25","x^2 − 10x − 25","x^2 + 25"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 25"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 10x − 25":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 10x − 25":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+5x and −5x cancel.","Conjugates give a^2 − b^2: x^2 − 25."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-basketball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A square inbound box has side (x + 9) feet. Expand (x + 9)^2 for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 18x + 81","x^2 + 81","x^2 + 9x + 81","x^2 + 18x + 18"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 18x + 81"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 81":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 9x + 81":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 18x + 18":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Square the whole sum; not x^2 + 81.","Middle term 2·x·9 = 18x. Answer: x^2 + 18x + 81."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-basketball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"Compare the conjugate pair (x + 4)(x − 4) of court widths. Expand it.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 16","x^2 + 8x − 16","x^2 − 8x − 16","x^2 + 16"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 16"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 8x − 16":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 8x − 16":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+4x and −4x cancel; no middle term.","Difference of squares: x^2 − 16."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-soccer-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A square corner of the pitch has a side of (x + 7) meters. Expand (x + 7)^2 to get its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 14x + 49","x^2 + 49","x^2 + 7x + 49","x^2 + 14x + 14"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 14x + 49"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 49":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 7x + 49":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 14x + 14":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["(x + 7)^2 = (x + 7)(x + 7); not x^2 + 49.","Middle term 2·x·7 = 14x. Answer: x^2 + 14x + 49."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-soccer-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"Two passing lanes are conjugates: (x + 3) and (x − 3). Expand (x + 3)(x − 3).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 9","x^2 + 6x − 9","x^2 − 6x − 9","x^2 + 9"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 9"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 6x − 9":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 6x − 9":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+3x and −3x cancel.","Conjugates give a^2 − b^2: x^2 − 9."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-soccer-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A square training grid has side (x + 8) meters. Expand (x + 8)^2 for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 16x + 64","x^2 + 64","x^2 + 8x + 64","x^2 + 16x + 16"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 16x + 64"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 64":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 8x + 64":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 16x + 16":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Square the whole sum; not x^2 + 64.","Middle term 2·x·8 = 16x. Answer: x^2 + 16x + 64."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-soccer-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"Compare the conjugate pair (x + 10)(x − 10) of field lengths. Expand it.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 100","x^2 + 20x − 100","x^2 − 20x − 100","x^2 + 100"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 100"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 20x − 100":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 20x − 100":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+10x and −10x cancel; no middle term.","Difference of squares: x^2 − 100."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-football-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A square section of the field has a side of (x + 5) yards. Expand (x + 5)^2 to get its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 10x + 25","x^2 + 25","x^2 + 5x + 25","x^2 + 10x + 10"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 10x + 25"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 25":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 5x + 25":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 10x + 10":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["(x + 5)^2 = (x + 5)(x + 5); not x^2 + 25.","Middle term 2·x·5 = 10x. Answer: x^2 + 10x + 25."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-football-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"Two route depths are conjugates: (x + 4) and (x − 4). Expand (x + 4)(x − 4).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 16","x^2 + 8x − 16","x^2 − 8x − 16","x^2 + 16"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 16"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 8x − 16":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 8x − 16":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+4x and −4x cancel.","Conjugates give a^2 − b^2: x^2 − 16."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-football-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A square end-zone drill area has side (x + 6) yards. Expand (x + 6)^2 for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 12x + 36","x^2 + 36","x^2 + 6x + 36","x^2 + 12x + 12"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 12x + 36"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 36":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 6x + 36":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 12x + 12":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Square the whole sum; not x^2 + 36.","Middle term 2·x·6 = 12x. Answer: x^2 + 12x + 36."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-football-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"Compare the conjugate pair (x + 11)(x − 11) of field positions. Expand it.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 121","x^2 + 22x − 121","x^2 − 22x − 121","x^2 + 121"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 121"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 22x − 121":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 22x − 121":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+11x and −11x cancel; no middle term.","Difference of squares: x^2 − 121."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-volleyball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A square serving zone has a side of (x + 3) feet. Expand (x + 3)^2 to get its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 6x + 9","x^2 + 9","x^2 + 3x + 9","x^2 + 6x + 6"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 6x + 9"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 9":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 3x + 9":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 6x + 6":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["(x + 3)^2 = (x + 3)(x + 3); not x^2 + 9.","Middle term 2·x·3 = 6x. Answer: x^2 + 6x + 9."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-volleyball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"Two attack distances are conjugates: (x + 8) and (x − 8). Expand (x + 8)(x − 8).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 64","x^2 + 16x − 64","x^2 − 16x − 64","x^2 + 64"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 64"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 16x − 64":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 16x − 64":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+8x and −8x cancel.","Conjugates give a^2 − b^2: x^2 − 64."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-volleyball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A square block-zone has side (x + 7) feet. Expand (x + 7)^2 for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 14x + 49","x^2 + 49","x^2 + 7x + 49","x^2 + 14x + 14"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 14x + 49"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 49":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 7x + 49":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 14x + 14":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Square the whole sum; not x^2 + 49.","Middle term 2·x·7 = 14x. Answer: x^2 + 14x + 49."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-volleyball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"Compare the conjugate pair (x + 2)(x − 2) of court depths. Expand it.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 4","x^2 + 4x − 4","x^2 − 4x − 4","x^2 + 4"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 4"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 4x − 4":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 4x − 4":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+2x and −2x cancel; no middle term.","Difference of squares: x^2 − 4."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-neutral-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A square tile has a side of length (x + 4). Expand (x + 4)^2 to get its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 8x + 16","x^2 + 16","x^2 + 4x + 16","x^2 + 8x + 8"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 8x + 16"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 16":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 4x + 16":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 8x + 8":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["(x + 4)^2 = (x + 4)(x + 4); not x^2 + 16.","Middle term 2·x·4 = 8x. Answer: x^2 + 8x + 16."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-neutral-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A rectangle has sides (x + 6) and (x − 6), a conjugate pair. Expand (x + 6)(x − 6) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 36","x^2 + 12x − 36","x^2 − 12x − 36","x^2 + 36"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 36"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 12x − 36":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 12x − 36":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+6x and −6x cancel.","Conjugates give a^2 − b^2: x^2 − 36."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-neutral-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A square garden bed has side (x + 9). Expand (x + 9)^2 for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 18x + 81","x^2 + 81","x^2 + 9x + 81","x^2 + 18x + 18"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 18x + 81"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 81":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 9x + 81":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 18x + 18":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Square the whole sum; not x^2 + 81.","Middle term 2·x·9 = 18x. Answer: x^2 + 18x + 81."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p1-neutral-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A rectangle has sides (x + 12) and (x − 12), a conjugate pair. Expand (x + 12)(x − 12).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 144","x^2 + 24x − 144","x^2 − 24x − 144","x^2 + 144"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 144"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 24x − 144":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 24x − 144":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+12x and −12x cancel; no middle term.","Difference of squares: x^2 − 144."],"difficulty":3}],"p2":[{"id":"ALG-P09-p2-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A scout models a square hit-zone of side (x + 7). On the area diagram, what is the middle (2ab) coefficient of (x + 7)^2?","visual":"area-model","answer":{"kind":"numeric","value":"14"},"misconceptionMap":{"0":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Middle term is 2·x·7, not 0.","2·7 = 14."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P09-p2-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A model writes the range factors as conjugates (x + 5)(x − 5). Expand to standard form.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 25","x^2 + 10x − 25","x^2 − 10x − 25","x^2 + 25"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 25"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 10x − 25":"conjugates-keep-middle","x^2 − 10x − 25":"conjugates-keep-middle"},"hints":["+5x and −5x cancel.","a^2 − b^2 = x^2 − 25."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p2-baseball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A stat sheet squares the binomial (x + 6). Write (x + 6)^2 in standard form.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 12x + 36","x^2 + 36","x^2 + 6x + 36","x^2 + 12x + 12"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 12x + 36"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 36":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 6x + 36":"square-of-sum-drops-middle","x^2 + 12x + 12":"square-of-sum-drops-middle"},"hints":["Not x^2 + 36; include the 2ab term.","2·x·6 = 12x: x^2 + 12x + 36."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P09-p2-baseball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P09","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A model uses conjugates (x + 9)(x − 9). Expand to standard form.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 81","x^2 + 18x − 81","x^2 − 18x − 81","x^2 + 81"],"answer":{